  "tool.heightpoint.title": "Height point",
  "@tool.heightpoint.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Height point\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a height (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a base point — an existing one is shared, empty space places a new one: the result is that point lifted off the sketch plane, with the height an ordinary parameter.",
    "x-translated": "14cbb0f5"
  },
  "tool.heightpoint.help": "Type a height (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a base point — an existing one is shared, empty space places a new one: the result is that point lifted off the sketch plane, with the height an ordinary parameter. In the 3D view you can grab it and drag the height; the base stays draggable where it was drawn.",
  "@tool.heightpoint.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Height point\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a height (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a base point — an existing one is shared, empty space places a new one: the result is that point lifted off the sketch plane, with the height an ordinary parameter.",
    "x-translated": "7b891872"
  },
