  "tool.projectplane.title": "Projected point",
  "@tool.projectplane.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Projected point\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Anchor a construction on this pane to a point defined on another.",
    "x-translated": "9e68cbc9"
  },
  "tool.projectplane.help": "Anchor a construction on this pane to a point defined on another. Click the point you want to project — it can live on any pane, so switch the sketch plane to reach it (the picks are kept), and an existing point is shared so the projection follows every edit to it. Then switch to the pane you want it projected onto and click anywhere on it: the point lands at the foot of the perpendicular dropped onto that plane, in the plane's own coordinates — not where you click. Use it as a circle's centre, a coil's axis, a weld target. Make absolute frees it in place if you want to detach it.",
  "@tool.projectplane.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Projected point\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Anchor a construction on this pane to a point defined on another.",
    "x-translated": "ad02e5ba"
  },
