  "tool.helixptleft.title": "Helix (centre, start point, left-hand)",
  "@tool.helixptleft.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Helix (centre, start point, left-hand)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: The same two clicks as Helix (centre, start point, right-hand) — an existing point is shared, empty space places a new one — turning the other way as it rises — a left-hand thread, a left-hand spring.",
    "x-translated": "c337c657"
  },
  "tool.helixptleft.help": "The same two clicks as Helix (centre, start point, right-hand) — an existing point is shared, empty space places a new one — turning the other way as it rises — a left-hand thread, a left-hand spring. Handedness is which tool you used, so it is what the file records and it never changes by itself; a negative pitch is refused, because a coil that descends while it turns right is this one.",
  "@tool.helixptleft.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Helix (centre, start point, left-hand)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: The same two clicks as Helix (centre, start point, right-hand) — an existing point is shared, empty space places a new one — turning the other way as it rises — a left-hand thread, a left-hand spring.",
