  "tool.intersectioncurve.title": "Intersection curve",
  "@tool.intersectioncurve.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Intersection curve\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: On a working plane, click the section of the body you want: the curve in space where that plane meets that solid becomes a curve like any other — sweep a tube along it, stand a station on it, carry a cut along it.",
    "x-translated": "5375b803"
  },
  "tool.intersectioncurve.help": "On a working plane, click the section of the body you want: the curve in space where that plane meets that solid becomes a curve like any other — sweep a tube along it, stand a station on it, carry a cut along it. A plane cuts a body in several curves in general (a bent bar is cut twice, a tube gives two loops); the one you click is the one you get, and that choice is remembered, so moving the plane afterwards never swaps to another curve. Move the body or the plane and the curve follows. The plan draws no section — open a working plane first.",
  "@tool.intersectioncurve.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Intersection curve\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: On a working plane, click the section of the body you want: the curve in space where that plane meets that solid becomes a curve like any other — sweep a tube along it, stand a station on it, carry a cut along it.",
    "x-translated": "6b1e7dd5"
  },
