  "tool.spherecircle.title": "Circle of two sphere loci",
  "@tool.spherecircle.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Circle of two sphere loci\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click two sphere loci: the circle in space where they meet — every point at both distances at once — becomes a curve like any other, so you can sweep along it, stand a station on it, or find where a third locus crosses it.",
    "x-translated": "aefefd8a"
  },
  "tool.spherecircle.help": "Click two sphere loci: the circle in space where they meet — every point at both distances at once — becomes a curve like any other, so you can sweep along it, stand a station on it, or find where a third locus crosses it. It is an exact circle, not a fit. Loci that are too far apart, one inside the other, or that merely touch say so and heal the moment a radius changes.",
  "@tool.spherecircle.help": {
