  "tool.sphereonrun.title": "Point where a run meets a sphere locus",
  "@tool.sphereonrun.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Point where a run meets a sphere locus\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click a sphere locus and then a route — a curve in space, or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: what you get is the place along that route which stands at the stated distance.",
    "x-translated": "baaf27b5"
  },
  "tool.sphereonrun.help": "Click a sphere locus and then a route — a curve in space, or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: what you get is the place along that route which stands at the stated distance. A route can be at that distance several times; the crossing you click nearest is the one you get, counted along the run, and that choice is remembered. A route that grazes the locus and turns back crosses it nowhere, and a route that no longer reaches it says so and heals.",
  "@tool.sphereonrun.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Point where a run meets a sphere locus\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"points\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click a sphere locus and then a route — a curve in space, or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: what you get is the place along that route which stands at the stated distance.",
    "x-translated": "1a364a4"
  },
