  "tool.extrudepoint.title": "Extrude to point (pyramid, cone)",
  "@tool.extrudepoint.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Extrude to point (pyramid, cone)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"solids\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a height (or pick a parameter in the panel), click an outline, footprint or circle, then click where its apex belongs: the area runs to that point — a pyramid from a polygon, a cone from a circle.",
