  "tool.loft.title": "Loft (sections)",
  "@tool.loft.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Loft (sections)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"solids\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click the sections in order — an outline, a wall footprint, a circle, or a point for an apex end — then press Enter (or click the first section again).",
    "x-translated": "599e7720"
  },
  "tool.loft.help": "Click the sections in order — an outline, a wall footprint, a circle, or a point for an apex end — then press Enter (or click the first section again). Sections may lie on different sketch planes: switch the plane between clicks and the picks are kept. An *open* curve among the picks is a guide the run follows, and it must pass through corresponding points of the sections it spans. Where you click on each section starts its boundary correspondence, so click near the corner that should meet the one you clicked before — the preview draws the rails.",
  "@tool.loft.help": {
