  "tool.tube.title": "Tube along a curve",
  "@tool.tube.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Tube along a curve\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"solids\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a radius (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a curve in space — or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: a round tube follows it — a cable, a conduit, a handrail.",
    "x-translated": "e2262f01"
  },
  "tool.tube.help": "Type a radius (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a curve in space — or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: a round tube follows it — a cable, a conduit, a handrail. Type a roll after the radius to turn the section about the run at its start, and a twist for the total turn from one end to the other. The curve stays live: drag a point it runs through and the tube follows. In the plan the tube shows the outline of its two sides, which is exactly where they are; an end face is closed by a straight line across it, and where the run points straight down into the plan you see the section itself. The radius may also be a **formula over the run**: type it into *Section law* in the panel (t runs from 0 at the start of the run to 1 at its end) and the tube tapers — `5mm * (1 - t/2)` is a handle half again as thin at its end, `2mm + 8mm*t*t` is a horn. The formula reads any parameter above it, so a tapered handle follows a dimension like everything else; it supersedes the typed radius.",
  "@tool.tube.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Tube along a curve\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"solids\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a radius (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a curve in space — or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: a round tube follows it — a cable, a conduit, a handrail.",
    "x-translated": "3162d0c9"
  },
  "tool.tube.slot.1": "curve in space",
  "@tool.tube.slot.1": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Tube along a curve\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"solids\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a radius (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click a curve in space — or a drawing, which is read as the run it already is: a round tube follows it — a cable, a conduit, a handrail.",
    "x-translated": "11d469d7"
