  "tool.chain.title": "Chain (cutting curve)",
  "@tool.chain.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Chain (cutting curve)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click the points the cut runs through, then press Enter: the first and last become rays, so the chain runs to infinity at both ends and separates the drawing into two sides.",
    "x-translated": "5b00b20e"
  },
  "tool.chain.help": "Click the points the cut runs through, then press Enter: the first and last become rays, so the chain runs to infinity at both ends and separates the drawing into two sides. Two clicks give an infinite line; each further click bends it. Cut or split a solid with it afterwards — or cut with a line you have already drawn, which is that same infinite line, or with any closed curve.",
  "@tool.chain.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Chain (cutting curve)\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"curves\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Click the points the cut runs through, then press Enter: the first and last become rays, so the chain runs to infinity at both ends and separates the drawing into two sides.",
