  "tool.chamfer.title": "Chamfer",
  "@tool.chamfer.title": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Chamfer\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"construct\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a chamfer distance (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click the two legs — lines, segments, circles or arcs — on the sides of the corner you want bevelled.",
    "x-translated": "8bed74ee"
  },
  "tool.chamfer.help": "Type a chamfer distance (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click the two legs — lines, segments, circles or arcs — on the sides of the corner you want bevelled. Like *Fillet*, the bevel **supersedes the corner**: both legs are trimmed back to its ends, and on two adjacent legs of an axis-aligned path it is that corner's own setback, read by the path's extrude, walls, key points and boundary. The distance is measured along each leg from the corner, which on a round leg means arc distance; the bevel is the straight segment between those two points.",
  "@tool.chamfer.help": {
    "description": "UI text of the \"Chamfer\" tool in ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program; toolbar section \"construct\". These strings are the tool's button label, the help sentence shown while it is armed, and the names of the things it asks the user to click. What the tool does: Type a chamfer distance (or pick a parameter in the panel), then click the two legs — lines, segments, circles or arcs — on the sides of the corner you want bevelled.",
