  "ui.formulas": "Formulas over t",
  "@ui.formulas": {
    "description": "Text of a field, button or tooltip in the Formulas section of the side panel of ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program that builds geometry as a dependency graph. The letter t is the run parameter of a curve or of a swept body, going from 0 at the start to 1 at the end.",
    "x-translated": "7d4b91b1"
  },
  "ui.formulas.title": "Formulas over the parameter t, both reading any value above. A curve piece: x(t), y(t) over a stated domain — an involute of the circle of radius r is x = r*(cos(t)+t*sin(t)), y = r*(sin(t)-t*cos(t)). A swept section's size law: r(t) for a tube, scale(t) for a profile, with t from 0 at the start of the run to 1 at its end.",
