  "ui.sectionlaw": "section law r(t) / scale(t) — e.g. 5mm * (1 - t/2)",
  "@ui.sectionlaw": {
    "description": "Text of a field, button or tooltip in the Formulas section of the side panel of ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program that builds geometry as a dependency graph. The letter t is the run parameter of a curve or of a swept body, going from 0 at the start to 1 at the end.",
    "x-translated": "9113f266"
  },
  "ui.sectionlaw.title": "A swept section's size along its run: one formula over t, which is 0 at the start of the run and 1 at its end. A tube reads it as the radius itself (5mm * (1 - t/2) is a tapered handle, 2mm + 8mm*t*t a horn); a swept profile reads it as a scale about the point it rides on (1 + t/2 is half again as large at the end). Select a swept body to see and change its own law; select nothing to arm the next Tube or Sweep.",
  "@ui.sectionlaw.title": {
    "description": "Text of a field, button or tooltip in the Formulas section of the side panel of ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program that builds geometry as a dependency graph. The letter t is the run parameter of a curve or of a swept body, going from 0 at the start to 1 at the end.",
