    "x-translated": "7ceea31b"
  },
  "ui.sectionlaw.apply.title": "State the size law: on the selected swept body, or armed for the next Tube or Sweep. Blank takes it away.",
  "@ui.sectionlaw.apply.title": {
    "description": "Text of a field, button or tooltip in the Formulas section of the side panel of ConstructIt, a parametric 2D/3D CAD program that builds geometry as a dependency graph. The letter t is the run parameter of a curve or of a swept body, going from 0 at the start to 1 at the end.",
    "x-translated": "f52f1adc"
  },
  "ui.familylaws.title": "A row per named parameter the selected section is built from, plus the run's own twist: give any of them a formula over t and the section is read once per station, so root and tip are genuinely different outlines. Select a swept body to see and change its own laws; select the section to arm the next Sweep.",
